+- `conversation_list` carries one authenticated user's own conversation metadata and no conversation content, and the user id it is read for is taken from the connection, never from a field of the frame, so a client cannot read another user's history by naming them ([validated by: answers a frame naming another user with the page of the user on the connection, with limit and before passed through](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L257)).
+- Decision: `transport.history` is the deployer's decision to make a user's conversation metadata reachable from their client, taken separately from `transport.resume` because resume only hands back a conversation the client was already in; the retention bound on that metadata stays the consumer's, as for resume ([session-resume](../hal-engine-session-resume/spec.md)).
 
